    {
      "@id": "#step-review_prior_work",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "computation",
      "name": "Retrieve prior literature (PMC OA full-text XML by default, broader via\nECAA_LIT_SOURCE_SCOPE) on the analysis's target entities + tissue +\nmodality. Emit a structured prior_claims_matrix.csv where every row is\nPMID-anchored with a substring-verified evidence_quote. No biological\nsynthesis, no narrative review.\n",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-validate_review_prior_work",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "validation",
      "name": "Validate outputs of: Retrieve prior literature (PMC OA full-text XML by default, broader via\nECAA_LIT_SOURCE_SCOPE) on the analysis's target entities + tissue +\nmodality. Emit a structured prior_claims_matrix.csv where every row is\nPMID-anchored with a substring-verified evidence_quote. No biological\nsynthesis, no narrative review.\n",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-data_acquisition",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "computation",
      "name": "Acquire raw experimental data from public repositories (SRA, GEO, ArrayExpress,\nENA, PRIDE, ClinVar, gnomAD, GTEx) or SME-supplied paths. Emits a cohort manifest,\nper-accession provenance summary, and an index pointing at the materialized\nartifacts. Downstream atoms consume the manifest, not the raw bytes directly.\n\nRECORD-WHAT-YOU-DID (audit, not instruction): if the source you actually read\nDIFFERS in any way from the source that was requested — the requested path or\naccession was absent, unreachable, embargoed, or served a different data form,\nand you fell back to a redistribution, a mirror, a bundled package, a\ndifferent accession, or locally generated data — write a `source_deviation`\nobject at the top level of result.json. This does NOT authorise a\nsubstitution and does NOT tell you which source to prefer; it says that if you\nsubstitute, you must state it. Record:\n  - requested: the source that was asked for, verbatim (path, accession, URL,\n    package name — whatever intake named).\n  - requested_available: true/false — was the requested source reachable at\n    the time you ran? false = the substitution was forced; true = you swapped\n    a source that WAS available.\n  - used: the source you actually read.\n  - used_kind: its class — one of package / accession / local_path / url /\n    mirror / synthetic, or another short label if none of those fits.\n  - used_version: the version, release, revision, or accession that pins\n    `used` (omit only when the substitute carries no version handle).\n  - reason: why you substituted, in one or two sentences.\n  - checksums: an object mapping each materialized input file (path relative\n    to your task output dir) to its sha256, so a reviewer can confirm which\n    bytes were analysed.\nWhatever you name in `used` MUST agree with the source your\nper_accession_summary.json describes — the harness cross-checks the two and\nblocks the task if they contradict. Do NOT write runtime/decisions.jsonl: the\nharness reads this block and appends the typed decision record itself. If you\nread exactly the requested source, OMIT the key entirely.\n",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-validate_data_acquisition",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "validation",
      "name": "Validate outputs of: Acquire raw experimental data from public repositories (SRA, GEO, ArrayExpress,\nENA, PRIDE, ClinVar, gnomAD, GTEx) or SME-supplied paths. Emits a cohort manifest,\nper-accession provenance summary, and an index pointing at the materialized\nartifacts. Downstream atoms consume the manifest, not the raw bytes directly.\n\nRECORD-WHAT-YOU-DID (audit, not instruction): if the source you actually read\nDIFFERS in any way from the source that was requested — the requested path or\naccession was absent, unreachable, embargoed, or served a different data form,\nand you fell back to a redistribution, a mirror, a bundled package, a\ndifferent accession, or locally generated data — write a `source_deviation`\nobject at the top level of result.json. This does NOT authorise a\nsubstitution and does NOT tell you which source to prefer; it says that if you\nsubstitute, you must state it. Record:\n  - requested: the source that was asked for, verbatim (path, accession, URL,\n    package name — whatever intake named).\n  - requested_available: true/false — was the requested source reachable at\n    the time you ran? false = the substitution was forced; true = you swapped\n    a source that WAS available.\n  - used: the source you actually read.\n  - used_kind: its class — one of package / accession / local_path / url /\n    mirror / synthetic, or another short label if none of those fits.\n  - used_version: the version, release, revision, or accession that pins\n    `used` (omit only when the substitute carries no version handle).\n  - reason: why you substituted, in one or two sentences.\n  - checksums: an object mapping each materialized input file (path relative\n    to your task output dir) to its sha256, so a reviewer can confirm which\n    bytes were analysed.\nWhatever you name in `used` MUST agree with the source your\nper_accession_summary.json describes — the harness cross-checks the two and\nblocks the task if they contradict. Do NOT write runtime/decisions.jsonl: the\nharness reads this block and appends the typed decision record itself. If you\nread exactly the requested source, OMIT the key entirely.\n",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-raw_qc",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "computation",
      "name": "Run sequencing QC (FastQC, MultiQC) on raw FASTQ inputs. Emits a per-sample metric\ntable and aggregated report; downstream `sequence_trimming` reads the trim-needed\nflag.\n",
      "position": 5
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-validate_raw_qc",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "validation",
      "name": "Validate outputs of: Run sequencing QC (FastQC, MultiQC) on raw FASTQ inputs. Emits a per-sample metric\ntable and aggregated report; downstream `sequence_trimming` reads the trim-needed\nflag.\n",
      "position": 6
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-survey_method_landscape",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "computation",
      "name": "Retrieve a context-scoped METHOD-LANDSCAPE for this analysis: for each\nruntime method-choice axis in the workflow, gather candidate methods and\nPMID/DOI/URL-anchored evidence, conditioned on the specific data\n(organism, protocol, sample count, missingness from the upstream QC +\nsample-manifest) and the analysis goal/modality. When the task carries\nan attributes.goal_context (the SME analysis goal), treat it as RETRIEVAL\nSCOPE — gather candidate methods + evidence relevant to that goal (e.g. a\nlow-allele-frequency / heteroplasmy detection goal widens retrieval toward\nAF-window-aware candidates). This conditions WHAT is retrieved only; it is\nnever a ranking or recommendation instruction. Honors\nconfig/downstream-policy/source-discovery-policy.json. Emit a\nmethod_landscape.csv where every row is locator-anchored with a\nsubstring-verified evidence_quote. No synthesis; no ranking (the\ndiscover_* atoms rank deterministically from this table).\n",
      "position": 7
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-discover_sequence_trimming",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "discovery",
      "name": "Discover method for sequence_trimming (options: trimmomatic, cutadapt, fastp, trim_galore). Surface set_intake_method.",
      "position": 8
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-discover_quantification",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "discovery",
      "name": "Discover method for quantification (options: salmon, kallisto, featurecounts, htseq, rsem). Surface set_intake_method.",
      "position": 9
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-discover_pathway_enrichment",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "discovery",
      "name": "Discover method for pathway_enrichment (options: fgsea, clusterprofiler, gsea, enrichr). Surface set_intake_method.",
      "position": 10
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-discover_normalisation",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "discovery",
