      "name": "Validate outputs of: Test pre-defined gene sets (KEGG / Reactome / GO / MSigDB hallmark) against\nranked DE results. fgsea / clusterProfiler / GSEA / enrichr selected at runtime.\n\nRanking gene sets needs an entity-label ↔ accession mapping (the DE table is\nkeyed by Ensembl accession; gene sets are keyed by symbol or Entrez id), so\nthis stage necessarily resolves one. Write it out as\nannotation/symbol_map.tsv — tab-delimited, header `symbol` then\n`ensembl_gene_id`, one row per distinct mapping, sorted by accession — under\nthis task's own output dir and NOT under intermediates/, which the deposit\nexport drops. This mapping comes from the pinned genome annotation\n(org.Hs.eg.db / biomaRt) rather than from the literature join, so it is the\nINDEPENDENT source the entity-label ↔ accession consistency check needs in\norder to catch a citation attached to the wrong entity.\n",
      "position": 41
    },
    {
      "@id": "#step-contextualize_findings_with_literature",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "additionalType": "computation",
      "name": "Map each row of the upstream findings table (DE genes / called peaks /\ncalled variants) to PMID-anchored prior-work rows. Emit\nclaims_evidence_matrix.csv with deterministic concordance flags\n(same_direction / opposite_direction / no_prior_finding / unverifiable /\nnot_assessed). No synthesis; no narrative.\n\nDO NOT hand-write this mapping. The package ships a tested, deterministic\nimplementation at runtime/literature/; call it and let it write every\ndeclared artifact:\n\n  python3 -m runtime.literature \\\n    --results      runtime/outputs/<upstream_stage>/<results_table> \\\n    --symbol-column <column holding the entity label> \\\n    --effect-column <signed-effect column> \\\n    --significance-column <adjusted-p column> \\\n    --threshold    0.05 \\\n    --prior-claims runtime/outputs/review_prior_work/prior_claims_matrix.csv \\\n    --evidence-manifest runtime/outputs/review_prior_work/evidence/manifest.json \\\n    --out-dir      runtime/outputs/contextualize_findings_with_literature \\\n    --entity-kind  gene|region|variant \\\n    --contrast-term <perturbation> [--contrast-term <synonym> ...]\n\nIt writes claims_evidence_matrix.csv, evidence/manifest.json,\nannotation/symbol_map.tsv, literature_search_protocol.md and\ncitation_verification_report.md, and prints a JSON summary on stdout to fold\ninto result.json. Run it from the package root. Column arguments are\noptional — omitted, each is resolved from a declared candidate list — but\nnaming them explicitly is preferred, and a named column that is absent from\nthe header is a hard error rather than a silent fallback to a different\nmeasurement.\n\nYOUR ONLY PREPARATORY STEP is the identity join: the library does not\nresolve identifiers, so if the results table has no entity-label column,\nadd one using the run's pinned annotation (see the gene-identity rule\nbelow) and pass it as --symbol-column. Write that joined table under this\ntask's own output dir, NOT under intermediates/ — the deposit export drops\nevery intermediates/ path, so a join left there is absent from the deposit.\nThe library then records the mapping it read as the declared artifact\nannotation/symbol_map.tsv (tab-delimited, header `symbol` then\n`ensembl_gene_id`, one row per distinct mapping, sorted by accession). Do\nNOT hand-write, rename, or post-edit that file, and do not invent a\ndifferent filename for it: it is the table the independent\nentity-label ↔ accession consistency check reads.\n\nThe library derives PMIDs, quotes, offsets, source hashes and prior\ndirections from the retrieved snapshots themselves, and the analysis\ndirection from the sign of the effect column. Do not pass any of them in,\nand do not post-edit the emitted CSV.\n",
      "position": 42
    },
    {
